The attached image (Fig. 5) illustrates that Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Panel A's flow cytometry plots show a higher percentage and mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA-positive cells in draining lymph nodes when OVA is formulated with Nano-11, compared to soluble OVA or OVA with aluminum hydroxide (AH), on both Day 1 and Day 2. Panel B quantifies that Nano-11 significantly increases the MFI of OVA per cell within OVA-containing cells. Panel C indicates that Nano-11 preferentially delivers antigen to migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among the OVA-positive cells, highlighting its specific targeting capability.